#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
"""Your way of working, across AI agents.

Model Citizen: a user-aligned, model-provider-agnostic harness built on shared custom primitives.

Projects shared primitives into selected runtimes, merges owned settings, renders personal
guidance, and reports drift. Python 3.9+ with a bundled style-preserving TOML parser.

    citizen init    [--force] [--yes]
    citizen install [--dry-run] [--no-brew] [--no-apps] [--no-vscode] [--no-codex] [--with-optional]
    citizen sync    [--dry-run] [--adopt] [--adopt-codex]
    citizen diff    [--quiet]
    citizen doctor
    citizen upgrade [--dry-run]
    citizen uninstall
    citizen lint    [PATH]
    citizen usage   [--days N] [--by day|repo|model|role|stance|decision|provider|prefix] [--stance NAME] [--rescan]
    citizen usage   --rules [--by rule|repo|stance] [--days N] [--rescan]
    citizen usage   --conflicts [--days N]
    citizen intent  claim PATH... | release | check [PATH...] | list [--all] | sweep
    citizen intent  merge [clean|conflicted] [--base REF]
    citizen worktree create NAME [REPO] [--branch BRANCH] [--base BASE] [--no-fetch]
    citizen worktree audit [REPO]
    citizen worktree remove NAME [REPO] [--merged] [--also-clear NAME]
    citizen workspace create NAME FOLDER... [--no-harness] [--force]
    citizen workspace list | open NAME [--codex] [--dry-run] [-- ARGS...]
    citizen config get KEY | set KEY VALUE
    citizen integrations show|register|doctor [architecture-viewer]
    citizen viewer validate|open|status|replace-document|close [OPTIONS]
    citizen integration check|apply NAME [REPO] [--force]
    citizen bmad    check|apply [REPO] [--force]   (alias for `integration ... bmad`)
    citizen remote-control install [--dry-run] | status | uninstall
    citizen --version

`harness` is a supported alias for `citizen`: the same program under its earlier name.
"""
